Overlay patch 0066 (VR R19 item 6): THE START-LINE LAKITU, PUSHED BACK TO
WHERE A CHASE CAMERA SEES HIM, IN VR FIRST PERSON ONLY.

the user on 1.0.0.17: "when you start a race, the cloud guy laikutu, he comes too
close to you, any way to fix that?"

WHY. The countdown Lakitu (unk_0D8 == 1, update_object_lakitu_starter) is
placed by OLakitu::func_8007A66C relative to the PLAYER's kart, rotated by the
game camera's yaw: pos = kart + R(yaw) * (origin_pos + offset), the offset
running a spline (D_800E67B8). Its size (sizeScaling 0.15) and its distance
were tuned for MK64's chase camera, which hangs well behind and above the kart.
In VR first person the eye sits AT the kart (the pinned seat, 3.2 u up), so
the same world position is several times closer to the eye than it is to any
flat camera: he hangs in the rider's face.

WHAT. After func_8007A66C places the starter (case 1 of func_8007AA44, and
ONLY that case -- the checkered-flag, lap-count, retrieval and reverse
Lakitus are untouched), when gSohVRFpWorld (shell: a VR world frame in
first person), gSohVRLakituPush and the starter is shown (object flag 0x10),
he is TRANSLATED by (seat - game camera), seat = kart + the pinned first-
person height (3.2 u, R18-B). So his offset from the rider's seat is exactly
his offset from MK64's chase camera: the same distance (~50-58 u through the
countdown hold, measured), the same bearing against the camera's look
direction, the same size on screen. The first attempt -- pushing him radially
out from the kart to the chase camera's distance -- was measured and dropped:
it kept his bearing FROM THE KART, which is steeply up and to the right
(az 25-58 deg, el 41-62 deg from the eye), i.e. out of the field of view.
Anchor = the seat, not the live eye: anchoring on the head would make him
follow every head movement. Third person, Diorama, 2D/3D-panel and every
flat frame: gSohVRFpWorld is 0, nothing moves (the flat path computes the
instrument only).

INSTRUMENT (bridge `vr lakitu`, all targets that link the shell): the
starter's distance and bearing from the game camera (`cam_d`, `cam_az`,
`cam_el`: the flat reference, read before any move), to the kart, to the VR eye (gSohVREyePosGame, VR world frames only), the camera-kart
distance, minima over the visible countdown, and the push count. RED/GREEN on
one binary: `vr set lakitupush 0` = 1.0.0.17.

Platform: __IOS__ (iPhone + visionOS); the macOS build compiles none of it.

REV2 (VR R20 item 2, 2026-10-09): CLOSER AND HIGHER. the user on 1.0.0.18:
"lakitu is now a little too far away, he's also too low, so that the racers
in front of me block him." rev1 put him at the chase camera's whole offset
(45-60 u, near eye level), where the grid rows ahead stand between him and the
rider. rev2 keeps the flat AZIMUTH (the offset's horizontal direction), scales
the offset by gSohVRLakituDistK (default 0.60 -> ~27-35 u through the hold),
and lifts him by gSohVRLakituUp game units above that point. The lift is
DERIVED, not tasted (docs/VR-R20-NOTES.md §2): from the rider's eye his lowest
point (pos.y - 35 * 0.15 = pos.y - 5.25: fixed_common_vtx_lakitu at
sizeScaling 0.15) must clear the top of the kart + driver sprite of the grid
row TWO places ahead (gPlayerVtx's quad, 18 u tall at gCharacterSize 0.75 =
13.5 u) by at least half a sprite height, as an angle:
    (bottom - eye) / dL >= (top2 + 6.75 - eye) / d2,
dL his horizontal forward distance from the seat, d2 that kart's. The
instrument measures d2/top2 on the live grid every countdown tick and reports
the clearance in sprite heights (`row2_clear_h`, >= 0.5 is the requirement).
Bridge knobs `vr set lakitudist <k>` and `vr set lakituup <u>`.


